# templates/understand-anything.gitattributes
#
# Apply these lines to the consuming repo's root `.gitattributes` (append if the
# file exists, create if it does not). They commit the Understand-Anything artifact
# (Point #1) while suppressing its diff in PRs and excluding it from language stats.
#
# Source of truth: workflows/repo-init.md §1 and templates/understand-anything-action.yml.
#
# Directory preference (Decision #3): `.ua/` is the current Understand-Anything
# default and the preferred location. The legacy `.understand-anything/` form is
# kept below as a fallback so existing repos still satisfy the #1 gate without a
# forced migration. New repos: use `.ua/`. Legacy repos: see the migration prompt
# in `skills/ws-repo-init/SKILL.md` Step 4 (`git mv .understand-anything .ua`).

# ---- Preferred: `.ua/` (current Understand-Anything default) ----
.ua/knowledge-graph.json binary -diff linguist-generated
.ua/**                 linguist-generated

# ---- Legacy: `.understand-anything/` (older Understand-Anything default) ----
# Keep these lines only while a legacy artifact dir is still in use. They are
# harmless when the `.ua/` lines above are also present (both can coexist during
# a migration window).
.understand-anything/knowledge-graph.json binary -diff linguist-generated
.understand-anything/**             linguist-generated

# Leave `.ua/config.json` (and the legacy `.understand-anything/config.json`) and
# any plugin manifests (`.claude-plugin`, `.cursor-plugin`, `.copilot-plugin`)
# committed as plain text — those are small, human-curated and SHOULD diff normally.
